  Get access  Request pilot access and have your administrator confirm your organization, project, role and application URL. Use the sign-in method configured for your workspace. A successful identity-provider login alone does not grant local project membership.    Capture and review a rule  Choose a recurring problem, such as tenant-scoped invoice queries. Record the intended behavior, affected paths, exceptions, supporting evidence and acceptance checks. Submit the proposal, then have an authorized reviewer approve it. With single sign-on turned on, someone other than the author must approve it.    Compile the next task  Supply the task, repository, files and technologies. The compiler selects applicable approved guidance and returns a persisted package. This example is a request body for  POST /v1/instructions/compile  on your provisioned API:   {
  &quot;project&quot;: &quot;your-project&quot;,
  &quot;task&quot;: &quot;Add a tenant-scoped invoice lookup&quot;,
  &quot;repository&quot;: &quot;your-team/your-repo&quot;,
  &quot;files&quot;: [
    &quot;app/invoices/routes.py&quot;
  ],
  &quot;technologies&quot;: [
    &quot;postgresql&quot;,
    &quot;fastapi&quot;
  ],
  &quot;budget_tokens&quot;: 2000
}   Use your assigned project and the technology labels attached to your rules. Check the response status and selection reasons. Resolve a blocked package before continuing.    Record what happened  Keep the package ID, run your required checks in your development environment, and record the observed outcome with evidence. A missing result is awaiting feedback, not a success. Compare with a similar baseline task when evaluating efficiency.
